<title>USA: Lawmakers introduce bill to curb unsolicited loans.</title>
<headline>Lawmakers introduce bill to curb unsolicited loans.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lenders would be prohibited from sending consumers unsolicited loans that look like checks under legislation proposed Wednesday in the House of Representatives.</p>
<p>Democrats Maurice Hinchey of New York and Henry Gonzalez of Texas introduced the bill, the Unsolicited Loan Consumer Protection Act of 1997, to curb the growing trend.</p>
<p>&quot;Banks should not be sending unsolicited loans through the mail where anyone can get their hands on them,&quot; Hinchey said.</p>
</text>
